# COA chromatogram auto-positioning

Uploaded HPLC chromatograms must use the established **auto positioning** every time — mild contain zoom so the chart fills the report box while keeping axes/sides visible.

## Source of truth

- Constant: `COA_CHROMATOGRAM_ZOOM` (`1.08`) in `src/lib/coaImages.ts`
- Display: `object-contain` + that zoom on `.coa-chrom-photo img` (`InteractiveChromatogram`)
- Print / PNG CSS: same `scale(1.08)` with a sync comment in `index.css`
- Digital PDF export: always apply `COA_CHROMATOGRAM_ZOOM` when re-painting `.coa-chrom-photo` images
- Template PDF: `drawContainedImage(..., COA_CHROMATOGRAM_ZOOM)`

## Do not

- Do **not** reintroduce aggressive `prepareHplcImage` trim + cover-crop pipelines for chromatograms (that broke display)
- Do **not** call full `paintLiveImagesOntoCanvas` after a successful html2canvas capture (re-painting vial + chromatogram overlays huge images across the COA). Success path may only use `paintChromatogramZoomOntoCanvas`.
- Do **not** drop the zoom from PDF export
- Do **not** zoom so hard that chart side axes disappear (stay near `COA_CHROMATOGRAM_ZOOM`, not ~1.22+)

## Intent

Auto-position once as the default for every COA chromatogram — screen and saved PDF must match.
